      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: Is std::span::data() really considered an unsafe buffer usage? It doesn\u0027t appear to be marked unsafe in the `base` equivalent, but for `std` I don\u0027t understand how unsafe annotations work. Anyway they seem totally wrong because `std::span(ptr, size)` should be unsafe but `std::span::data()` shouldn\u0027t be, which we\u0027ll fix when we switch everything to our own span.\n\n(I think I\u0027ve seen this too, but I don\u0027t really know why because the definition of std::span doesn\u0027t seem to say anything about it. Must be built into the plugin somewhere - or maybe this is something that triggers only in clangd? I\u0027ve seen that it catches some stuff that the actual build doesn\u0027t.)",
